---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageIntro from '../components/PageIntro.astro';
import Privacy from '../content/privacy.mdx';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Colophon"
  description="A small, static website built with Astro, TypeScript, and MDX, designed for readability, accessibility, and simple maintenance."
>
  <PageIntro
    label="Colophon"
    title="A small site, built with care."
    description="A few decisions behind the pages you’re reading."
  />
  <article class="prose colophon-prose">
    <h2>Content first</h2>
    <p>
      I built this site with Astro and strict TypeScript. Work, research, and
      lab entries live in schema-validated MDX collections, keeping the writing
      separate from the layouts.
    </p>
    <h2>Focused interaction</h2>
    <p>
      Most pages are static HTML. A small React component powers the regression,
      classification, and evaluation workspace in the lab; its explanatory
      content and initial results appear in the static page. A separate React
      island on the Ask page provides an optional public-content assistant;
      submitting a question is a deliberate action.
    </p>
    <h2>Readable by design</h2>
    <p>
      The design uses system serif and sans-serif fonts, a quiet neutral
      palette, and a green accent. Keyboard access, visible focus, contrast, and
      smaller screens are part of the design.
    </p>
    <Privacy />
    <h2>Attribution & responsibility</h2>
    <p>
      Professional descriptions draw on my public profile and firsthand project
      experience. Research contributions link to their sources, and
      demonstrations use synthetic data. Contact me about reusing writing or
      identity materials; consult the original sources for third-party material.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
